ads.</p><details class="ev-story-drawer"><summary>Read Bespoke Architectural Story &amp; Monograph ▾</summary><div class="ev-story-content"><h4>The Country-House Two-Tone Dresser Reborn: SIENA 120 with Timber Worktop &amp; Integrated Dual Sockets</h4><p class="ev-story-lead">Every British kitchen lover knows the enduring charm of a classic white dresser with a warm timber worktop—and every home barista knows the frustration of trailing extension leads across a wall. SIENA 120 solves both in one 120-centimetre architectural cabinet with two flush-mounted power sockets.</p><p>In so many period and suburban British kitchens, a 90-centimetre cabinet feels slightly too compact for a full espresso setup plus a microwave or food mixer, while a 170-centimetre credenza is simply too wide for the wall. Measuring 120 centimetres wide by 45 centimetres deep and 208 centimetres high, SIENA 120 hits the golden middle ground. Dressed in a crisp matt white membrane over 18-millimetre Grade-A full MDF and contrasted with a warm natural timber-finish preparation worktop and full-height wood-grained back panel, it bridges classic British country-kitchen warmth with smart modern engineering.</p><p>Look inside the wide 120-centimetre preparation alcove and you immediately spot two features that transform daily convenience: first, a touch-sensor daylight LED lighting bar recessed neatly beneath the upper glazed cabinets; second, a dual flush-mounted power socket module integrated directly into the cabinet structure. That means your espresso machine and burr grinder—or your coffee maker and toaster—plug straight into the coffee station itself without a tangle of trailing cables snaking down behind the plinth. Above the 41.5-centimetre-tall timber-backed alcove, three clear-glazed shaker-profiled upper doors display your mugs, teapots, and glassware across two internal shelf tiers.</p><p>Below the warm timber worktop, SIENA 120 offers the generous drawer-and-cupboard rhythm of a proper Welsh dresser. Two side-by-side soft-close drawers on damped telescopic steel runners allow you to separate coffee pods, tampers, and tea accessories on the left from cutlery, napkins, and baking tools on the right. Beneath the twin drawers, three classical panelled lower cupboard doors—each finished with tactile antique-brass-toned cup handles—open to reveal cavernous larder storage crafted entirely from moisture-resistant 18-millimetre full MDF.</p><ul class="ev-story-highlights"><li>120 × 45 × 208 cm two-tone kitchen &amp; coffee dresser combining matt white 18 mm membrane MDF with a warm timber-finish worktop and back panel.</li><li>Built-in dual flush-mounted power sockets and touch-sensor LED task lighting—eliminating trailing appliance leads for espresso machines and grinders.</li><li>Three clear-glazed upper display doors, two side-by-side damped telescopic drawers, and three panelled lower larder cupboards with classic cup handles.</li></ul><a href="/coffee-corners/toscana-93-plinth/" class="ev-story-page-link">Open Dedicated TOSCANA 93 PLINTH Product Page →</a></div></details><ul class="ev-badges"><li>2 Integrated Sockets</li><li>Touch-Sensor LED</li><li>93 cm Compact</li><li>Membrane MDF</li></ul><div class="ev-dims"><div><small>Width</small><b>93 cm</b></div><div><small>Depth</small><b>45 cm</b></div><div><small>Height</small><b>208 cm</b></div></div><p class="ev-counter-note">61 cm worktop clearance · 2 integrated sockets · Touch-sensor LED</p><a href="/coffee-corners/toscana-93-plinth/" class="ev-detail-page-btn">View Full Product Story &amp; Specifications →</a><div class="ev-actions"><div><label for="ev-q-23">Qty</label><input id="ev-q-23" class="ev-qty" type="number" value="1" min="1" max="100" step="1" inputmode="numeric"/></div><button type="button" class="ev-add">Add to Quote List <span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></button></div><button type="button" class="ev-direct ev-card-wa-btn" data-card-id="ev-ev-24">Add &amp; Send Quote via WhatsApp (+44 7898 